From: Caboose <caboose@local>
Subject: [PATCH 78/90] Compile trace scopes away without a tracer

MESA_TRACE_SCOPE formatted its name into a 4 KiB stack buffer with vsnprintf on every
call, tracer or not: every Vulkan entry point of the driver paid it, thousands of times
a frame, and Zink's teardown of a lost device spent its time there. Built without
Perfetto, GPUVis or Sysprof (as the driver is), a scope is now nothing.
---
diff --git a/src/util/perf/cpu_trace.h b/src/util/perf/cpu_trace.h
index 60c0382..3cff898 100644
--- a/src/util/perf/cpu_trace.h
+++ b/src/util/perf/cpu_trace.h
@@ -95,7 +95,9 @@ struct mesa_trace_flow {
 
 #endif /* HAVE_SYSPROF */
 
-#if __has_attribute(cleanup) && __has_attribute(unused)
+/* Without a tracer a scope is nothing: it would otherwise format its name on every call. */
+#if __has_attribute(cleanup) && __has_attribute(unused) && \
+   (defined(HAVE_PERFETTO) || defined(HAVE_GPUVIS) || defined(HAVE_SYSPROF))
 
 #include <stdarg.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
